    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 3.1: The 2012 Public Elections Act and the 2016 National Civil Registration Acts reviewed and harmonised to facilitate seamless link between the CR and the VR databases.

Public Elections Act &amp; Civil Registration Act reviewed and harmonised;
- At least five (5) regional consultations held;
- Draft Bill finalised;
- 1 national CRVS commemoration event held.

Output 3.2: NCRA has software environment for data exchange with NEC
Target: 
- ETL layer established in CRVS Data

Output 3.4: Public awareness of the importance of CRVS and its links to election voter registration process improved through an effective and decentralized information, education and communication campaign.

-10 materials in 6 ethnic languages reproduced;
- 17 town hall meetings;</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">-5 Consultative and inclusive process of review of Civil Registration Act (2016) supported
-Draft data protection policy, bill and regulation ongoing through an inclusive process via 5 regional consultative &amp; 1 national validation sessions
-NCRA is being supported with databases and software including ETL, connectivity &amp; Data synchronization layer to enable automated transfer of data with other national institutions such as the Electoral Commission
-Community awareness conducted in 16 districts targeted 30 participants including market women, community health workers, school children, traditional and religious leaders per district.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">16 informal community engagement held for awareness raising
20 local registrars and 20 regional staff capacitated in new policies, acts and regulations.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
    </period>
